# Synvitta engagement scope

Read `Synvitta-Case-Background.md` and `PrimarySources/CORE-INFORMATION.md` before substantive
work. Check `Framing/STATUS.md` and `Research/STATUS.md` for what is locked vs open.
Governing sources: case PDF + prompt-card draft under `PrimarySources/company/`.

## What this engagement is

U.S. market entry for **Synvitta Diagnostics**. The case names **three** opportunities; the team
recommends **ONE** first move, with customer/partner, route, and a 90-day plan.

| Option in case | Near-term character |
|---|---|
| SynELISA™ research kits (TSH, T4, syphilis Abs) | RUO; not for patient diagnosis |
| SynArray™ newborn screening | Late-stage; future clinical path needs development/validation/regulatory |
| SynArray™ custom panels (e.g. SynHormone™) | Collaborations / paid co-development |

End deliverable shape (when solving is requested) — see `Deliverables/deliverable-check.md`:

- One opportunity, one customer  
- Approach and regulatory assumption to verify  
- Three actions, 2–3 prospects  
- Two metrics, one risk  
- 3–5 slides

## Decisions and next steps

**Default until STATUS says otherwise:** frame, issue, problem statement, opportunity, customer,
how, and 90-day plan are **undecided**. Do not write as if they were locked.

**When the team announces a decision:** follow `.cursor/rules/decision-routing.mdc` — confirm,
update STATUS, point to the **immediate** next steps only, list what remains open.

**MECE is core** — `.cursor/rules/mece.mdc`. Overlaps and gaps are findings.

## Hard outs — refuse and redirect

| Out of scope | Redirect to |
|---|---|
| FDA filing strategy / legal opinions | Questions to verify (case instruction) |
| Detailed financial forecast | Speed-to-revenue and readiness comparisons only |
| Nationwide market sizing | Account/partner fit and route credibility |
| Three full business plans | One priority opportunity |

## Phase ladder

| Phase | Allowed | Open next when… |
|---|---|---|
| Prepare / framestorm | Facts, rival frames, support/challenge | Frame/problem announced |
| Problem statement | Five tests + 90-day move + value of being right | PS locked |
| Issue tree / research | MECE tree, priorities, vetted answers | Root cause can be stated |
| Root cause → claim | “This is the root cause…” then falsifiable claim + rival | Claim drafted |
| Analysis test | Branch-tied work plan; peers/segments; data ladder (`.cursor/rules/analysis-test.mdc`) | Claim survived or revised |
| Plan / solve | One opportunity, customer, how, 90-day | Explicit ask **after** analysis |

## Source discipline

- Tag material claims **RETRIEVED** or **ESTIMATED**.
- Do not invent Synvitta product, customer, or regulatory facts.
- Drinkware / Charter artifacts are method practice only.
